  "airline": "JBU",
  "name": "Vets in Blue (JetBlue Honors Our Veterans)",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "A320",
  "description": "Fuselage: Navy all over, belly included. Cheatlines: A gold ribbon: one tail of it starts at the belly behind the nose gear, runs aft along the lower fuselage under the wing, widening, and rises behind the wing to the fin root; the other, short tail crosses the tail cone under the tailplane. Tail: Navy fin with the ribbon's big open loop in gold and orange-gold, a navy hole in the middle, touching the leading and trailing edges; navy above it. Engines: Navy with white 'jetblue.com', polished lips. Winglets: Gold wingtip fences. Titles: White 'jetBlue' forward; 'JETBLUE HONORS OUR VETERANS' in small white italic capitals above the windows behind the wing; 'Vets In Blue' small under the cockpit. Artwork: the yellow-ribbon motif (the tail is the ribbon's loop, not a flag). America250 markings were reported for 2026 but no 2026 photo was found.",
